Save this as `index.html` to play **Dune Loop**, a low-poly Three.js time trial. Use **WASD** or the **arrow keys** to drive and **R** to reset. Your first forward crossing starts the timer. Each full lap updates your best time, which the game saves in the browser when local storage is available.

**Implementation notes, from static review:** The track is an annulus. The car stores its position, heading, and speed. The lap tracker stores the previous angle, signed progress, and start time. This follows **Model the domain**: reversing subtracts progress, so crossing the finish line back and forth cannot count as a lap. I chose an annulus over a spline so the road, barriers, and lap logic can share the same geometry without a track editor or physics library.

**Throughput checkpoint:** Define the track and timing rules first. Rendering and lap logic can be reviewed independently. Only the frame loop updates race state. Keep the implementation in one file because there is no build step or asset pipeline.

