      model.rotation.y = -a + car.steer * 0.22;

      const { x, z } = model.position;
      behind.set(x - dx * 9, 5.7, z - dz * 9);
      target.set(x + dx * 5, 0.75, z + dz * 5);
      camera.position.lerp(behind, snap ? 1 : 1 - Math.exp(-8 * dt));
      camera.lookAt(target);

      lapText.textContent = time(race.startedAt === null ? 0 : now - race.startedAt);
      bestText.textContent = race.best === null ? '--:--.---' : time(race.best);
      status.textContent = race.startedAt === null ? 'Press W or ↑ to start' :
        Math.abs(car.offset) > track.halfWidth - 0.7 ? 'Shoulder · reduced speed' :
        race.notice || 'Lap in progress';
      renderer.render(scene, camera);
      requestAnimationFrame(frame);
    }

    resize();
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### How I would verify it

Open `index.html` in a desktop browser with internet access. If the browser blocks the module on a `file://` URL, serve the file over localhost. For example, with Python installed, run `python -m http.server 8000` in the file's directory and open `http://localhost:8000`.

| Check | Expected result |
|---|---|
| Load the page and open the developer console. | The car, track, and HUD appear with no console errors. The timer stays at zero before input. |
| Hold W from the starting position without steering. | The car follows the centerline. One loop on a responsive tab should take about eight seconds, estimated from the speed and track length. The best lap appears and the live timer rolls over. |
| Press R, reverse across the stripe with S, then use W to cross it forward again. | Neither crossing awards a lap. The car still needs a full forward loop from the starting position. |
| Steer onto the shoulder, then back onto the road. | The car moves laterally, slows on the shoulder, and can accelerate again on the road. |
| Complete a slower lap, press R, then reload at the same URL. | The slower lap does not replace the record. R clears the current attempt, and the best lap survives the reload when storage is enabled. |
| Resize the window and switch tabs while holding a key. | The view resizes without stretching, and the key does not stay pressed when you return. |

